OBTW
  LOLCODE (Adam Lindsay, 2007): the language of the lolcats, these
  pictures of cats with captions in broken English ("I CAN HAS
  CHEEZBURGER?"). Every program starts with HAI and ends with KTHXBYE.

  The words used here:
  - CAN HAS STDIO? asks for the standard library, politely;
  - I HAS A ... ITZ ... declares a variable with its value;
  - VISIBLE prints its arguments, glued together, then a new line;
  - BTW starts a comment; a long one, like this one, sits between
    O-B-T-W and T-L-D-R (spelt out here: the real word would end it).

  Run it with lci, the reference interpreter:

      lci hello.lol
TLDR

HAI 1.2
  CAN HAS STDIO?

  BTW WHO GETS TEH RENDEZ-VOUS
  I HAS A WHO ITZ "you"
  I HAS A WHAT ITZ "a rendez-vous"

  BTW TEH SAME LINE, GLUED
  VISIBLE "I give " WHO " " WHAT "!"
KTHXBYE
